'' --diagnostics-file named by a '#cmdline' in the source: the source wins, as it does for
'' every option, so the records go to the file IT names.
''
'' The command line's file is still created -- pass one's DiagOut.Start creates it empty
'' before the restart is known -- and is left empty, which a reader takes as "did not
'' finish" rather than as a build with nothing to report.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --diagnostics-file build/.diagfile-outer.tsv --parse-only tests/driver/src/diagfile-directive.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-inner.tsv :: \t#print inner\nend\t0\t0\t0\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.diagfile-outer.tsv :: tiko-diagnostics
